{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01JO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$a : T \\to V$", "MATH_0003": "$b : T \\to W$", "MATH_0004": "$f \\circ a = g \\circ b$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$T \\to X \\times_S Y$", "MATH_0008": "$p^{-1}(V) \\cap q^{-1}(W)$", "MATH_0009": "$p^{-1}(V) \\cap q^{-1}(W)$", "MATH_0010": "$V$", "MATH_0011": "$W$", "MATH_0012": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-section-fibre-products}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:283c5e3c37f0d18e87a2fa15bda7163537f35b05b922f2ed6ff8bb7dfc0fea48", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c06fcaf675432772baa14f082e5a77c4f6889173e21f439d3a6c341690d5b9e8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nSuppose <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> are morphisms\nsuch that <MATH_0004> as morphisms into <MATH_0005>.\nThen they agree as morphisms into <MATH_0006>.\nBy the universal property of the fibre product we get\na unique morphism <MATH_0007>. Of course this morphism\nhas image contained in the open <MATH_0008>.\nThus <MATH_0009> is a fibre product of\n<MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011> over <MATH_0012>. The result follows from the uniqueness\nof fibre products, see Categories, Section\n<REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4f68d898008a13a099ea73cdc57c1b2f0f8257ef0c23388b00deef8578930e35", "unit_id": "tag:01JR:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01JO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V \\times_U W = V \\times_S W$", "MATH_0002": "$U, V, W$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\times_U W$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\times_S Y$", "MATH_0005": "$V \\times_U W$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:46347c6c30550599b3e48dd4c1335adbd7281c3985dc1370da2ec0a50fbf0a78", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a1db7a3a307f73084e4e120a46d15dd97b7397efcceeab4acfae13f722b0bab1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn particular this shows that <MATH_0001>\nin the situation of the lemma. Moreover, if <MATH_0002> are all\naffine, then we know that <MATH_0003> is affine. And of course\nwe may cover <MATH_0004> by such affine opens <MATH_0005>.\nWe formulate this as a lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bae9c4124a0f7616cbdb2401af1f440e9c2ea2d7df7e34b6c9354ad45156e61c", "unit_id": "tag:01JO:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01JO", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nBare-hands construction of fiber products: an affine open cover of a\nfiber product of schemes can be assembled from compatible\naffine open covers of the pieces.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$S = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$i \\in I$", "MATH_0006": "$f^{-1}(U_i) = \\bigcup_{j \\in J_i} V_j$", "MATH_0007": "$f^{-1}(U_i)$", "MATH_0008": "$g^{-1}(U_i) = \\bigcup_{k \\in K_i} W_k$", "MATH_0009": "$g^{-1}(U_i)$", "MATH_0010": "$$\nX \\times_S Y =\n\\bigcup\\nolimits_{i \\in I}\n\\bigcup\\nolimits_{j \\in J_i, \\ k \\in K_i}\nV_j \\times_{U_i} W_k\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$X \\times_S Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-affine-covering-fibre-product}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5b7c7adab9a4700cbc3aadc11ad12c44665a0ef7747cbdbb4a66213add2f8fca", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aa38d5b5b092be61dd926272dfbaa84a2e84118bb55e5bb2d594ba7b750ff2d1", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be morphisms of schemes\nwith the same target. Let <MATH_0003> be any affine open\ncovering of <MATH_0004>. For each <MATH_0005>, let\n<MATH_0006> be an affine open covering\nof <MATH_0007> and let\n<MATH_0008> be an affine open covering\nof <MATH_0009>. Then\n<MATH_0010>\nis an affine open covering of <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9319cfe276d479a88fcad19c7c409cc2ef31df60faf6fb26d22b8b86bffd8de3", "unit_id": "tag:01JS:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01JO", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9c524ab90f2080be3523107598f77c66dc9342fb402fb6c13a4992c8696c4ae9", "source_text": "See discussion above the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a01b088bf209a6134feedb992b3845b918ef0a8c4245f07e2500f5c0623654d3", "unit_id": "tag:01JS:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01JO", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fibre-products}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6f0ff5ddb7716dd593dc30f98ac50db9968e0e194ecd28f1dc7a8ee6121dd870", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn other words, we might have used the previous lemma to construct\nthe fibre product directly by\nglueing the affine schemes. (Which is of course exactly\nwhat we did in the proof of Lemma <REF_0001> anyway.)\nHere is a way to describe the set of points of a fibre product of schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fbe2fd36daafd64f89d0bdf98a64303d22ca44b9543a9dfc198c0da0e1b3a0e9", "unit_id": "tag:01JO:prose-0004"}
